ion and permission budget, does not enter the setup workflow, and accepts a newly\n.change-loop\\fresh-suite\\H04-stale-datasheet-plan\\plan.md-79-     submitted plan for the new stable bytes;\n.change-loop\\fresh-suite\\H04-stale-datasheet-plan\\plan.md-80-  3. changing one byte after an incomplete primary call but before `board_fix_setup` makes the\n--\n.change-loop\\fresh-suite\\H04-stale-datasheet-plan\\plan-review.md-16-\n.change-loop\\fresh-suite\\H04-stale-datasheet-plan\\plan-review.md-17-**PROCEED**\n.change-loop\\fresh-suite\\H04-stale-datasheet-plan\\plan-review.md-18-\n.change-loop\\fresh-suite\\H04-stale-datasheet-plan\\plan-review.md:19:The stated one-definition change is sufficient. `definition_for_action(\"board_fix_setup\")` returns the `board_setup` definition, so setting `artifact_binding_field=\"datasheet_path\"` and `artifact_binding_suffixes=(\".pdf\",)` uses the existing binding for both the primary and paired calls. On execution, the engine verifies that binding before scope/precondition work and before decrementing allowance or consuming permission; an artifact refusal invalidates the shared plan and relocks its primary and paired actions. The guarded dispatcher runs this enforcement before either setup handler enters its workflow.\n.change-loop\\fresh-suite\\H04-stale-datasheet-plan\\plan-review.md-20-\n.change-loop\\fresh-suite\\H04-stale-datasheet-plan\\plan-review.md-21-## Execution risks and test targets\n.change-loop\\fresh-suite\\H04-stale-datasheet-plan\\plan-review.md-22-\n.change-loop\\fresh-suite\\H04-stale-datasheet-plan\\plan-review.md:23:1. **Declarative wiring:** Assert the `board_setup` definition exposes exactly `artifact_binding_field=\"datasheet_path\"` and `artifact_binding_suffixes=(\".pdf\",)`, and that the accepted public payload contains the existing byte-binding/replacement-plan reminder. Do not add a setup-specific binding implementation.\n.change-loop\\fresh-suite\\H04-stale-datasheet-plan\\plan-review.md:24:2. **P